course: dictionary
lesson: 4150
title: Glum and the shades of sad
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words mean almost the same thing, but not quite. «Glum, sad, miserable and heartbroken all mean unhappy, but each a different amount.» Glum is a quiet, gloomy kind of sad. You can look glum without shouting or crying.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. A character who has bad news, goes quiet and has a glum face is not crying and not angry. The clues show that glum means sad and quiet, looking unhappy and disappointed.
explain: Try the word in the sentence. «Sam had a glum face after he lost the game.» Does it still make sense if you put sad and quiet in its place? Yes, so you have found its meaning.
fact: Glum means sad and quiet, looking unhappy and disappointed.
fact: «Glum» can describe a face, a mood or a person: «a glum face», «feeling glum», «look glum».
fact: «Glumly» is the adverb: it tells you how someone did something, as in «He answered glumly».
fact: Glum is a quiet, gloomy sort of sad. Miserable is very unhappy, and heartbroken is the saddest of all.
fact: Glum is not the same as angry. Angry is hot and loud, while glum is quiet and low.
exercise: «Sam had a glum face after he lost the game.» What does glum show? | Sam was loud and rude | Sam was jumping with joy | *Sam looked sad and quiet, and disappointed | Sam was fast asleep
exercise: Priya says glum means the same as angry. Is she right? | Glum is a kind of food | Glum means the same as happy | Yes, glum always means angry and loud | *Not quite: glum means sad and quiet, not angry
exercise: «He answered glumly.» What does glumly mean? | With a big happy smile | *In a sad, quiet, unhappy way | Very quickly and loudly | In a cold, wet way
test: «Glum, sad, miserable and heartbroken all mean unhappy, but each a different amount.» Which of these is the saddest of all? | Sad | Miserable | *Heartbroken | Glum
test: Mia's dad says, «Your face looks glum, love.» What does he mean? | Very angry and shouting | *Sad and quiet, a bit unhappy | Full of energy and ready to run | Very hungry for dinner
exam: Which sentence uses glum correctly? | The glum rocket zoomed to the moon | The glum child laughed and danced all day | Glum is a fast car that won the race | *After the bad news, the glum child sat alone and said nothing
